# The audio path on the G4, with audio enabled (no --noaudio)
#
# Captured 2026-09-13 on the Power Mac G4 (Leopard 10.5.4, Radeon 9000) with
#     ./MarioParty4.app/Contents/MacOS/isle --frames 900 --gxwarn --stub-trace
# i.e. deliberately WITHOUT --noaudio, to record what the audio path actually
# does on big-endian hardware.  This is the specification hand-off for M6.
#
# WHAT IT SHOWS
#
# 1. msmSysInit SUCCEEDS on the G4.  There is no failure, no hang in HuAudInit,
#    and --noaudio is not needed: the boot runs all the way to the title screen
#    with the sound manager live.  src/msm (Hudson's own sound manager, 3,201
#    lines of pure C) reads /sound/mpgcsnd.msm correctly, because the file is
#    big-endian and so is the machine.  On the little-endian development host
#    the same parse rejects the bank's version field as 0x02000000.  Nothing
#    about that was ever fixable in audio code; it is the same 32-bit
#    big-endian story as the sprite banks (PLAN.md §10.6).
#
# 2. There is NO dspSlave command list to log yet, and this is why.  MusyX's
#    DSP command list is built by extern/musyx's hw_dspctrl.c (2,147 lines) and
#    handed to the DSP through hw_dolphin.c, and **extern/musyx is not in the
#    build**.  Every one of the 52 snd* entry points is a generated stub, so
#    nothing downstream of sndInit exists to emit a command batch.  M6's first
#    task is therefore not "interpret the DSP command list" but "compile
#    extern/musyx above the SAL and write port/src/audio/musyx_sal.c"; the
#    command list appears the moment that happens, and hw_dspctrl.c is its own
#    specification.
#
# 3. The snd* first-call order below IS the M6 implementation order.  18
#    distinct entry points, and they fall into three groups:
#
#      init      sndIsInstalled, AIInit, sndSetHooks, sndInit,
#                AIRegisterDMACallback, sndOutputMode, sndVolume
#      aux       sndAuxCallbackPrepareReverbHI, sndAuxCallbackPrepareDelay,
#                sndSetAuxProcessingCallbacks
#      streams   sndStreamAllocEx, sndStreamMixParameterEx, sndStreamFrq,
#                sndStreamADPCMParameter, sndStreamARAMUpdate, sndStreamActivate
#      banks     sndPushGroup
#
# 4. THE FIRST SOUND IS A STREAM, NOT A SEQUENCE.  The first sound the game
#    asks for is `>>>>>>>>MSM_SE_SEL_01 0` / `>>>>>>>>SE Num 0` -- the title
#    screen's selection effect -- and what it reaches is the five sndStream*
#    calls, twice.  That is msmstream.c's ADPCM streaming path into ARAM, not
#    the sequencer.  So the first thing M6 has to make audible is the ADPCM
#    stream, and the sequencer/voice/ADSR machinery can come after it.
#
# 5. `***********GroupSet Error -32` is HuAudSndGrpSetSet(0) failing because
#    sndPushGroup is a stub returning 0.  It is the game noticing, politely,
#    that no sample group was loaded.  It does not stop the boot.
#
# The full narration follows.

